heuristic. The audit measures and reports the raw HTML payload size from the fetched source."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"How do third-party scripts affect landing page speed?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Each third-party script (ad pixel, chat widget, review aggregator, A/B test framework) adds a DNS lookup, a connection, and a script execution. Loading four synchronously in the head can add 800ms-2s before the page begins rendering. The fix is to load non-critical scripts asynchronously or defer them after first contentful paint."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"What is Cumulative Layout Shift and why does it hurt conversion?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"CLS measures how much the page layout shifts while loading. When images load without declared width/height attributes, they collapse to zero height and then expand - pushing content down as they load. A visitor targeting the CTA button clicks on something else because the button moved. Google's CLS threshold is 0.1."}]]}]]}]]}]
